sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    actor User as Operator
    participant CLI as Rust CLI
    participant Journal as Request journal
    participant API as AnkiConnect v1
    participant Web as AnkiWeb
    participant Phone as AnkiDroid
    User->>CLI: sync demo-01
    CLI->>API: readiness + verify the existing note
    CLI->>Journal: persist attempt before sending
    CLI->>API: collection.sync(session, includeMedia=false)
    API-->>CLI: operationId (accepted, not completed)
    CLI->>Journal: save handle, request latency, sync_requested
    API->>Web: native Anki collection synchronization
    loop Until terminal state or timeout
        CLI->>API: operations.get(operationId)
        API-->>CLI: queued / running / terminal / waitingForUser
    end
    alt succeeded and collectionComplete=true
        CLI->>Journal: sync_confirmed + observation timestamp
        User->>Phone: explicitly sync
        Phone->>Web: download changes
        Web-->>Phone: new card
        User->>Phone: inspect both sides and Unicode
        User->>CLI: confirm-phone demo-01 --observed
        CLI->>Journal: separate human observation timestamp
    else failed or cancelled
        CLI->>Journal: terminal failure, explicit retry may follow repair
    else waitingForUser
        CLI->>Journal: waiting_for_user
        Note over User,API: Stop automated writes, administrative conflict recovery
    else timeout or lost response
        CLI->>Journal: failed_unknown, preserve any received handle
        Note over CLI,Journal: No new sync submission until the prior outcome is known
    end
